        lab:{title:'Map a five-node graph',task:'Model one product capability, user task, approved claim, evidence source, and owner. Add typed edges and identify which properties are required for trust.',deliverable:'A graph sketch plus three questions it can answer more reliably than page search alone.'},
        checklist:['Nodes have stable identities','Edges use specific verbs','Time and provenance are modeled where relevant','The graph supports named user questions','The model avoids relationships that no workflow uses'],
        check:{q:'When does a knowledge graph add the clearest value?',options:['When every page needs a title','When answers depend on traversing explicit relationships','When files need a new color scheme','When semantic search already solves every task'],answer:1,explanation:'Graphs are strongest when the task depends on explicit, typed, multi-hop relationships that text similarity alone cannot reliably infer.'}
