        concepts:[['Groundedness','The degree to which answer claims are supported by supplied evidence.'],['Entailment','Whether the evidence logically supports the specific claim made.'],['Coverage','Whether all consequential claims have sufficient evidence.'],['Abstention','A controlled decision not to answer when evidence, permission, or confidence is inadequate.']],
        body:['A citation can be present and still fail. It may link to a relevant page that does not support the claim, cite only part of a compound statement, or point to an outdated version.','Evaluate at the claim level. Break answers into factual units, map each unit to evidence, verify authority and applicability, and require abstention or qualified language when support is incomplete.'],
