        concepts:[['Evaluator prompt','Instructions, evidence, criteria, scale anchors, and output schema for the judging model.'],['Calibration set','Expert-labeled examples used to measure evaluator agreement and bias.'],['Pairwise evaluation','Comparing two responses on defined criteria rather than assigning an absolute score.'],['Evaluator drift','A change in judgments caused by model, prompt, context, or distribution changes.']],
        body:['Model evaluators are useful for criteria such as completeness, clarity, groundedness, or task fit when deterministic rules are insufficient. They are not a substitute for clear criteria or expert calibration.','Constrain the judge with the user task, source evidence, one criterion at a time, explicit anchors, and structured output. Measure agreement with experts and revalidate when the judge model or evaluation distribution changes.'],
