        check:{q:'What most improves the reliability of an LLM evaluator?',options:['Asking if the answer is generally good','Using a larger font','Specific criteria, anchored scales, and expert calibration','Hiding the source evidence'],answer:2,explanation:'Clear criteria and anchors reduce ambiguity; calibration reveals whether the judge agrees with trusted human decisions.'}
