        concepts:[['Source failure','Missing, wrong, stale, contradictory, or unauthorized knowledge.'],['Retrieval failure','Eligible evidence exists but is not selected, ranked, or assembled correctly.'],['Generation failure','The model misuses adequate context or violates task constraints.'],['Control failure','Evaluation, review, escalation, or release policy fails to prevent harm.']],
        body:['A failure taxonomy must lead to action. Categories should map to owners, evidence, and remediation—not merely describe that the answer was bad.','Assign the primary cause to the earliest controllable failure. A generation error may be downstream of ambiguous evidence; a retrieval miss may be downstream of missing metadata. Track contributing causes separately.'],
        workflow:['Capture the question, answer, context, citations, versions, and telemetry.','Identify the first layer where expected behavior diverged.','Classify primary and contributing causes.','Assign an owner, corrective action, and regression test.','Analyze patterns across incidents and prioritize systemic fixes.'],
